# Cargo.lock IS committed here on purpose (SEC-3899): pinning the fuzz crate's
# dependency graph keeps nightly builds reproducible and blocks a malicious
# newly-published version from being pulled unreviewed. Enforced by
# `cargo fetch --locked` in fuzz.yaml. Update via a PR-reviewed bump.
# The repo-root .gitignore ignores every Cargo.lock (lib workspace convention),
# so re-include this fuzz crate's lock explicitly.
!Cargo.lock

# Live, mutable libFuzzer corpus — never committed. Read-only seeds live in
# `seeds/`.
/corpus
